{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836400",
      "title": "More Examples: When To Use Refs & State",
      "sourceHash": "793b4e7ae167006417bd056740d20f6b65cb8c677f21c77eb0784dda427b5284",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.78,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "So now that we have an elegant way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 5.67,
          "en": "of showing this result modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.67,
          "end": 7.8,
          "en": "from inside the timer challenge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 8.81,
          "en": "it's time to enhance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.81,
          "end": 12.364,
          "en": "this timer challenge component a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.364,
          "end": 16.92,
          "en": "Because my goal is to not just say you lost here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.92,
          "end": 19.02,
          "en": "but to also show this modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.02,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "if we successfully stop the timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 24.813,
          "en": "and to then show a score in that modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.98,
          "end": 27.42,
          "en": "And to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.42,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "it's not enough to just set and stop a timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "Instead, we need to measure how much time is left",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 37.23,
          "en": "on an ongoing basis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.23,
          "end": 40.56,
          "en": "so that we know exactly how much time is left",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.56,
          "end": 42.603,
          "en": "when the timer is being stopped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 47.373,
          "en": "And setTimeout doesn't give us that information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.39,
          "end": 50.973,
          "en": "Therefore, instead, we need setInterval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 56.13,
          "en": "which is another function built into JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.13,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "or built into the browser to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 64.73,
          "en": "Now, setInterval works differently than setTimeout, though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 70.59,
          "en": "because setInterval will execute this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.59,
          "end": 74.43299999999999,
          "en": "every time this time here expired, so not just once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "And therefore, of course here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 80.13,
          "en": "I don't wanna set the targetTime as a time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.13,
          "end": 82.28999999999999,
          "en": "but a very short duration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 85.803,
          "en": "so that I can keep track of how much time expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.725,
          "end": 89.923,
          "en": "We could, for example, execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.923,
          "end": 91.86,
          "en": "every millisecond",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.86,
          "end": 93.727,
          "en": "but that would be a lot of executions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.727,
          "end": 96.944,
          "en": "and maybe not great for performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.944,
          "end": 100.28999999999999,
          "en": "Therefore, here I'll go for 10 milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.28999999999999,
          "end": 103.436,
          "en": "but you can play around with that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.436,
          "end": 106.38,
          "en": "Now in here, I, of course now don't wanna mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.38,
          "end": 108.39,
          "en": "this timer as expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.39,
          "end": 110.87299999999999,
          "en": "Instead, now we should totally change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.87299999999999,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "which states we manage here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 115.203,
          "en": "and we should instead simply keep track",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.203,
          "end": 118.263,
          "en": "of the remaining time in our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.97,
          "end": 122.569,
          "en": "So I'll get rid of these two state values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.569,
          "end": 125.043,
          "en": "and instead register a new state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.15,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "which is my remaining time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 131.849,
          "en": "or time remaining as I'll name it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.849,
          "end": 134.763,
          "en": "and the respective updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.16,
          "end": 139.94,
          "en": "Now, initially that should be the targetTime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.78,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "Though I want the targetTime in milliseconds here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "since this interval executes every 10 milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 153.03199999999998,
          "en": "and I wanna update this time remaining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.03199999999998,
          "end": 156.06,
          "en": "every 10 milliseconds, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.06,
          "end": 159,
          "en": "Hence, I'll set the initial time in milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 162.69299999999998,
          "en": "So the targetTime multiplied with 1000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 166.02,
          "en": "And then in here in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.02,
          "end": 169.47,
          "en": "which is executed every 10 milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.47,
          "end": 172.68,
          "en": "we should update the remaining time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.68,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "by calling setTimeRemaining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 180.003,
          "en": "and deduct 10 milliseconds from the current time remaining.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "So here, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "we should use this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 190.52,
          "en": "where we get the previous time remaining automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.52,
          "end": 194.13,
          "en": "and where we then return the new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.13,
          "end": 196.23,
          "en": "that should be set as a state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.23,
          "end": 200.373,
          "en": "And that's my previous time remaining -10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.21,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "So we have to deduct 10 milliseconds here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 207.32999999999998,
          "en": "so that in the end, this state here gets updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.32999999999998,
          "end": 211.353,
          "en": "every 10 milliseconds with the updated time remaining.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.39,
          "end": 216.75,
          "en": "And we should get rid of set timer started here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.75,
          "end": 219.06,
          "en": "Because instead now we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.06,
          "end": 221.89,
          "en": "that the timer is active, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.05,
          "end": 226.95499999999998,
          "en": "if timeRemaining is greater than zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.95499999999998,
          "end": 231.333,
          "en": "and smaller than the targetTime times 1000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.87,
          "end": 238.26,
          "en": "Because if it's smaller, we know that the timer is started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.26,
          "end": 240.09,
          "en": "Otherwise it would be equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.09,
          "end": 242.673,
          "en": "because that's our initial timeRemaining.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 245.756,
          "en": "And if it's smaller than zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.756,
          "end": 249.288,
          "en": "we know that the timer also shouldn't be treated as active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.288,
          "end": 253.589,
          "en": "because it expired because the targetTime is up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.589,
          "end": 255.99,
          "en": "Now of course, this interval here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.99,
          "end": 259.395,
          "en": "should still be stopped if handledStop is executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.395,
          "end": 261.753,
          "en": "so if this stop button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 266.25,
          "en": "But we can't clear an interval with clear timeout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.25,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "instead, we have to use clear interval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 270.363,
          "en": "which is also built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 274.02,
          "en": "And just as the setTimeout function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.02,
          "end": 276.789,
          "en": "setInterval also returns a reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 276.789,
          "end": 279.87,
          "en": "which we can store in our ref here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.87,
          "end": 282.345,
          "en": "and which we can then use to clear it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.345,
          "end": 285.984,
          "en": "And we still need to use a ref here and not a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.984,
          "end": 290.64,
          "en": "and not some state for the same reasons as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.64,
          "end": 293.94,
          "en": "So with that, we can still stop this timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 293.94,
          "end": 296.73,
          "en": "but now I also wanna stop it manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.73,
          "end": 298.23,
          "en": "if it expired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 298.23,
          "end": 300.813,
          "en": "not just if the stop button was pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 302.1,
          "end": 305.58,
          "en": "And therefore, here, right in the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.58,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "we can add a if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 312.41,
          "en": "and check if timeRemaining is smaller or equal to zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.52,
          "end": 317.91,
          "en": "Because if it is equal to zero or smaller,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 317.91,
          "end": 321.453,
          "en": "we know that time's up, that there is no time left.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 322.59,
          "end": 325.29,
          "en": "But set interval won't stop on its own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 325.29,
          "end": 328.078,
          "en": "because it has no end date, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.078,
          "end": 332.444,
          "en": "it just keeps on firing every 10 milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 332.444,
          "end": 335.37,
          "en": "So we also have to clear this interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 335.37,
          "end": 338.49,
          "en": "if we determine that the time is up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 338.49,
          "end": 341.211,
          "en": "which is the case, if the timeRemaining is zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 341.211,
          "end": 343.023,
          "en": "or smaller than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 348.45,
          "en": "Therefore in here, we then also want to call clearInterval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 348.45,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "and clearourtimer.current here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 353.65,
          "en": "so this interval which we set here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 354.63,
          "end": 357.693,
          "en": "so that this interval does not keep on executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 359.771,
          "end": 362.34,
          "en": "In addition here, in this if condition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 362.34,
          "end": 364.77,
          "en": "I'll then also set time remaining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 364.77,
          "end": 369.153,
          "en": "back to my initial targetTime times 1000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 370.012,
          "end": 372.21,
          "en": "Now setting the state like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 372.21,
          "end": 375.54,
          "en": "directly in a component function can be dangerous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 375.54,
          "end": 379.53,
          "en": "because you can create an infinite loop with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.53,
          "end": 382.56,
          "en": "Because setting the state causes the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 382.56,
          "end": 384.33,
          "en": "to execute again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 384.33,
          "end": 388.35,
          "en": "which could cause this function here to run again and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 388.35,
          "end": 390.3,
          "en": "But since I'm in a if condition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 390.3,
          "end": 393.93,
          "en": "which will not be met after updating the state like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 393.93,
          "end": 398.22,
          "en": "we are safe and this will not cause an infinite loop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 398.22,
          "end": 401.471,
          "en": "But it's important to be aware of this potential danger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 401.471,
          "end": 405.3,
          "en": "you are facing when calling a state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 405.3,
          "end": 407.73,
          "en": "from directly in your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 407.73,
          "end": 409.62,
          "en": "as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 409.62,
          "end": 413.168,
          "en": "But if you have a condition like this, everything's good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 413.168,
          "end": 416.853,
          "en": "Now with that, we also have to adjust the JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 417.99,
          "end": 421.98,
          "en": "And down here, I for example, want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 421.98,
          "end": 424.14,
          "en": "that for this button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 424.14,
          "end": 426.69,
          "en": "we trigger the handle stop function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 426.69,
          "end": 430.89300000000003,
          "en": "if the timer is active and handle start otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 432.03,
          "end": 435.06,
          "en": "And here we also want to use timer is active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 435.06,
          "end": 437.223,
          "en": "and also here and here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 439.35,
          "end": 442.56,
          "en": "So that we're using this new derived state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 442.56,
          "end": 444.57,
          "en": "this new computed value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 444.57,
          "end": 446.853,
          "en": "to update the UI appropriately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
